<title>GREECE: GREEK INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT DOWN 0.2PCT Y/Y IN DECEMBER.</title>
<headline>GREEK INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT DOWN 0.2PCT Y/Y IN DECEMBER.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek industrial production fell</p>
<p>provisionally 0.2 percent year-on-year in December after a 0.9</p>
<p>percent increase in November and manufacturing output dropped</p>
<p>2.9 percent year-on-year, the National Statistics Service (NSS)</p>
<p>said.</p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	 DEC 96*  NOV 96**  DEC 95</p>
<p>    Percent change(yr/yr)    -0.2	0.9	  1.5</p>
<p>    Index (1980=100)	  102.4    115.6	102.6</p>
<p>    MANUFACTURING OUTPUT    DEC 96*  NOV 96**  DEC 95</p>
<p>    Percent change(yr/yr)    -2.9%     0.1	   2.6</p>
<p>    Index (1980=100)	   91.8    107.8	  94.6</p>
<p>*  indicates provisional data</p>
<p>** indicates revised data</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
